<title>UK: Stagecoach falls after news of share placing.</title>
<headline>Stagecoach falls after news of share placing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK transport group Stagecoach Holdings fell on Tuesday after broker UBS said it planned to sell up to 35 million shares in the company.</p>
<p>The shares were 20-1/2p lower at 779p by 0857 GMT after earlier touching a low of 775p.</p>
<p>UBS said that former shareholders of Porterbrook which was acquired last year by Stagecoach, planned to sell their 14.6 percent stake in the transport group.</p>
<p>The disposal has been agreed by Stagecoach and the shares will be placed with institutions following an Accelerated Global Tender by UBS.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
